commit 25a64393e7e58a5570f142e87b17331adf8d7d15

C03: a pause conditioned on an application being open reads its window first (MUSIC1675)

«si tengo spotify abierto pausalo» conditions the pause on Spotify's present state; the deferred-effect reader treated every «si …» as a wait for a future event and the request stayed undecided. A condition on the present state of an application (open or not) is now read, not awaited: the request decides window.resolve on that application followed by media.control pause on its session, so an absent window ends the mission truthfully and a present one pauses that session. The direct-request gate sees through the condition (and «pausalo»/«pausame» are request heads), the window.resolve argument comes from the condition, and the pause pattern accepts the clitic forms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


